    {
      "id": "christ",
      "title": "Christ",
      "short": "Forty days without food, and he sits as if lost in thought.",
      "extended": "Mark’s Gospel gives the scene two short verses: after his baptism, Christ was in the wilderness forty days, tempted by Satan, with the wild beasts, while angels served him. Moretto shows no struggle. Christ rests his head on his hand, a gesture long used in art for meditation and for melancholy.",
      "references": [
        "Mark 1:12–13",
        "Matthew 4:1–2",
        "The Met, 11.53"
      ],
      "evidence": "documented",
