      "id": "stag",
      "title": "The Stag",
      "short": "“As the hart panteth after the water brooks…”",
      "extended": "A stag crosses the slope at the left. The deer was a familiar Christian image of the soul seeking God, taken from Psalm 42. Whether Moretto meant that here, or simply painted the animals of a wild place, cannot be settled from the picture alone.",
      "references": [
        "Psalm 42:1"
      ],
