      "id": "fox",
      "title": "The Fox",
      "short": "One of Mark’s wild beasts, resting a few steps from the serpent.",
      "extended": "The Met’s catalogue lists foxes among the painting’s animals. No single symbolic meaning fits them securely here; they belong, with the bear and the deer, to the wild beasts Mark says were with Christ.",
