      "id": "bear",
      "title": "The Bear",
      "short": "A dark shape lying in the grass, as quiet as everything else.",
      "extended": "The Met’s catalogue lists a bear among the painting’s animals. Predators lying at rest near grazing animals recall Isaiah’s peaceable kingdom, where the wolf lives with the lamb and the bear feeds beside the cow. That echo is a reading, not something the painting states.",
