    {
      "id": "fragment",
      "title": "The Missing Picture",
      "short": "These faint cherubs mark where a larger painting was cut away.",
      "extended": "The Met describes the canvas as a fragment of a larger work that once continued past the sketchy cherubim at the left and showed other events from Christ’s life. It has been suggested that Moretto’s Christ Blessing Saint John the Baptist, now in London, came from the same composition, though the National Gallery notes that the figures differ in scale.",
      "references": [
        "The Met, 11.53",
        "National Gallery, London, NG3096"
      ],
